          "content": {
            "id": "77d8b9d0-3550-335c-aab0-80de665633fe",
            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "Didi posts Q2 loss of $350 million on lawsuit provision, despite revenue growth",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Chinese ride-hailing giant Didi Global reported on Thursday a second-quarter net loss of 2.5 billion yuan ($350 million), driven by a one-off charge, even as revenue rose 10.9%, partly fuelled by growth in overseas business. The loss was largely due to a provision of 5.3 billion yuan for a previously disclosed shareholder lawsuit, while spending on marketing and other expense also increased, reflecting intensifying domestic competition. Didi maintains its dominant position in China's ride-hailing sector, but pressure from rivals is mounting.",
