            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "Chinese firms in legal battle over Brazil food delivery",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "SAO PAULO (Reuters) -A Brazilian subsidiary of China's ride-hailing company DiDi Global sued Chinese rival Keeta on Monday in a Sao Paulo court alleging trademark infringement and unfair competition, according to court documents seen by Reuters.  The lawsuit comes days after Keeta, which is entering the Brazilian market, sued DiDi's Brazilian unit, 99, in Brazil, alleging its food delivery app 99Food was trying to\u00a0restrict restaurants from working with more than two delivery platforms.  In Monday's lawsuit, 99 accused Keeta, owned by Chinese delivery giant Meituan, of using colors, graphics and font similar to 99's platform to \"catapult its commercial operations\" in the Brazilian market.",
